    "issue_context": {
        "number": 100174,
        "title": "ESQL: Remove aliasing inside Eval",
        "body": "### Description\n\nEvals that introduce aliased can be simplified by extracting them into a project (and thus signaling there's no underlying processing).\r\n\r\nThe following eval:\r\n`eval x = a + 1, y = x, z = y + 1, y = z, w = y + 1`\r\ncan be converted into:\r\n`eval x = a + 1, z = a + 1 + 1, w = a + 1 + 1 | project x, z, z as y, w`\r\n\r\nThis helps fuse the project with other projections/aggs downstream.",
        "comments": [
            "Pinging @elastic/es-ql (Team:QL)",
            "Pinging @elastic/elasticsearch-esql (:Query Languages/ES|QL)"
        ]
    },
